{#
  T-3.10 — the floating WhatsApp button.

  Included once from `master.twig`, after the footer, so it is the last thing in
  the tab order on every page — which is the "sensible position" the criterion
  asks for. A persistent utility that is not part of the page's content should
  not sit in front of the page's content in the tab order.

  THE NUMBER IS THE STORE'S, NOT A THEME SETTING, AND THE BACKLOG'S "number"
  FIELD IS DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT. `store.contacts.whatsapp` is where a merchant
  already keeps it, and a theme setting beside it would be a second place to
  write one fact — two sources that disagree the first time somebody changes the
  number in the obvious place. What IS a theme setting is whether the button
  appears at all, which the store has no opinion about.

  NO BUTTON WITHOUT A NUMBER. If the merchant has not set one, there is nothing
  to link to and the whole thing is omitted rather than rendered dead — the same
  rule T-4.22's two actions follow.

  The `replace` is upstream's own, from `thank-you.twig`: `wa.me` takes digits
  only, and a merchant types the number the way people write numbers.
#}
{#
  SECOND PASS, 2026-08-12 — colours, a side, and an optional label.

  THE LABEL CHANGES THE ACCESSIBLE NAME, AND THAT IS THE ONE SUBTLE PART. With
  no label the button is an icon in a circle and `aria-label` is the only name it
  can have. **With a label, keeping the `aria-label` would override the visible
  text** — a screen reader would announce «تواصل عبر واتساب» while the button
  reads «راسلنا», and WCAG 2.5.3 (Label in Name) is precisely about those two
  not disagreeing. So the attribute is emitted only when there is no visible
  text to name the control.
#}
{% set whatsapp_label = theme.settings.get('whatsapp_fab_label') %}
{% set whatsapp_side = theme.settings.get('whatsapp_fab_side', 'end') %}

{% if theme.settings.get('whatsapp_fab_enabled', true) and store.contacts.whatsapp %}
    <a class="whatsapp-fab whatsapp-fab--{{ whatsapp_side }}"
       href="https://wa.me/{{ store.contacts.whatsapp|replace({' ': '', '+': '', '-': '', '(': '', ')': ''}) }}"
       target="_blank"
       rel="noopener noreferrer"
       data-whatsapp-fab
       data-side="{{ whatsapp_side }}"
       {% if not whatsapp_label %}aria-label="{{ trans('theme.common.whatsapp') }}"{% endif %}>
        {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'whatsapp', size: 'xl' } only %}
        {% if whatsapp_label %}
            <span class="whatsapp-fab__label">{{ whatsapp_label }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </a>
{% endif %}
